## Implementation Details

### Framework Detected
- Next.js 16.2.6 with App Router

### Installation Method (from official docs)
According to the latest Vercel documentation, the setup requires:
1. Installing `@vercel/speed-insights` package
2. Adding `<SpeedInsights />` component to root layout

### Current Implementation in app/layout.tsx
```typescript
import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/next'

// ... in the return statement:
{process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' && (
  <>
    <Analytics />
    <SpeedInsights />
  </>
)}
```

This implementation follows the official documentation and best practices by:
- Using the correct import path (`@vercel/speed-insights/next`)
- Placing the component at the end of the body tag
- Only loading in production environment
- Using the App Router pattern with the root layout

## Notes
- No environment variables are required for Speed Insights
- The component will automatically enable tracking after deployment to Vercel
- Data collection begins when users visit the deployed site
- Speed Insights routes will be available at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` after deployment

The project is ready for deployment with Speed Insights fully configured.
